    "notes": "Ro/ro vessel built in 1971 as Juno (registered in Finland). Sold, renamed and re-registered numerous times before being registered in the UK as the vessel Hascosay on 1 May 2002. Northlink Ferry between Aberdeen-Kirkwall-Lerwick Freight(2004 - 2010). Used to collect data for the JCDP during 2004. Previous names include Sea Clipper (from May 2001); Transbaltica (from Mar 1998); Sea Clipper (from Oct 1996); Commodore Clipper (from Jan 1991); Euro Nor (from May 1990); Misida (from Nov 1986); Normandia (from Jun 1979) and Juno (from Oct 1975). Became ABOU KARIM I (LB) in 2010, total loss in 2020.",
